{
  "title": "T2 Alpha® Humerus Nailing System",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423321/t2-alpha-r--humerus-nailing-system",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 22 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The T2 Alpha Humerus Nailing System is indicated for humeral shaft and proximal humerus fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The system maximizes rotational and axial stability across varying bone qualities through versatile locking configurations and a minimally invasive insertion technique.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "It streamlines surgical efficiency and OR logistics by utilizing a standardized single core tray that is compatible across the entire Gamma4® and T2 Alpha® platforms.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Stryker Orthopedic Modeling and Analytics (SOMA) designed",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "straight nail design allows for alignment of the epiphyseal fragment with the diaphysis and gives structural support to the humeral head fragment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "proximal screw trajectories are designed to aim for dense bone to reduce the potential of displacement of the humeral head",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "diameters defined through the SOMA database cover a wide range of intramedullary canal diameters in the analyzed population",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Active intraoperative compression",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "up to 6mm of controlled compression for long nails",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "designed to allow for a more controlled reduction of the fragments when compared to the traditional backslapping/backstroke method",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Guided targeters",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "targeters available for every hole except the distal lateral to medial",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Unique instrumentation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nail height stop: facilitates precise nail depth placement, while reducing the risk of nail protrusion through the proximal humerus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "cuff spreading device: designed to reduce the potential for rotator cuff damage",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Advanced locking screws",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "designed to provide increased axial fracture stability in any 4mm round locking hole when the surgeon chooses",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hybrid locking configuration designed for fixation of varying fracture patterns",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "greater tuberosity landmark",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "humeral shaft diaphysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "distal humerus flare",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Muscles",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "anterolateral split",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "supraspinatus entry interval",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "proximal landmark",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
